      "cooked": "<p>How does It, Yeah, I’m that Guy combo effectively with Twist the Ether? I don’t get the effects I’d expect in the video game.</p>\n<p>Suppose Visionary plays Twist the Ether on Tachyon, and Guise high-fives Tachyon. I would expect that either (1) Tachyon effectively has two Twist the Ethers on her, because Uh, Yeah is copying every card in her play area, or (2) Guise effectively has a Twist on him, because Uh, Yeah is copying the text of Twist but Guise is the target that Twist is “next to.” On the table, I’d rule it one of those two ways.</p>\n<p>In the video game, I got…no effect from high-fiving either Tachyon or Visionary. Is there a way to get Uh, Yeah to combo up with Twist?</p>",
